  m_Name: Day3Dad
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Category: 2
  Prefab: {fileID: 6625514644646704096, guid: 1f6a6789373206e498f996cb54aeedb1, type: 3}
  Interactable: {fileID: 5048261325816738630, guid: 1f6a6789373206e498f996cb54aeedb1, type: 3}
  TextFields:
  - Dear Astrid,
  - "Things at the South Pole are the same. Bright all day, every day. No nights.
    Cold. Getting IceCube back online is a lot of work\u2014but the good kind. After
    two years of backup generators, stale rations, and a million games of cribbage,
    I\u2019m glad to be doing real science again.\r\n\r\nYou asked what happened
    with the CME. Normally we shut the grid down\u2014standard drill. The first burst
    wasn\u2019t anything unusual. We got the alert, powered down. Just space weather.\r\n\r\nBut
    then the second wave hit. No warning. Stronger, faster. It struck right as systems
    were coming back online. Total overload. Nature doing its thing\u2014a rare one-two
    punch from the sun.\r\n\r\nSome people warned this could happen. One of them
    - Dr Thaddeus Zelensky -  who built the satellite Elijah\u2019s been trying to
    connect to. Most of us thought he was just eccentric. He died early on, but left
    the project to Elijah. He was right about that... not sure about getting satellite
    back online though. \r\nThe auroras are caused by CME activity, but after the
    blackout, they freak people out. People don\u2019t trust the sky. Most of the
    worst rumors, stories, even superstitions are about the heavens now. \r\n\r\r\nWe\u2019re
    lucky IceCube was offline when the second wave hit. That's why we got it back
    online. Thankfully the backup generators held or I would be a popsicle right
    now. \r\n\r\nGot to go, Little Bear. I love you. I love seeing the work you\u2019re
    doing. You're pretty incredible. "
  - Love, Dad
  StreamingVisuals: []
